    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "The pattern here is worth pointing out directly: most tools in this space specialize in one stage of the SEO process. Rext AI and, to a lesser extent, Semrush are the only ones that genuinely span research through publishing, and Rext AI is the only one that pairs that full workflow with a free tools library and direct CMS publishing at a flat, predictable price.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "How to Choose the Right Tool for Your Budget",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Monthly Budget",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 1,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Recommended Approach",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 1,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
          ],
          "type": "tablerow",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "$0 (testing phase)",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Start with Rext AI's free tools at rext.ai/tools, plus Ubersuggest or Ahrefs Webmaster Tools, to handle basic keyword research and technical SEO checks at no cost.",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
          ],
          "type": "tablerow",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Under $50",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Rext AI's entry plan or Frase for research and briefs, paired with free technical tools for sitemaps, schema, and meta tags.",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
          ],
          "type": "tablerow",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "$50–150",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Rext AI for the full workflow, or Semrush/SE Ranking if you specifically need deep competitor and backlink data alongside content tools.",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
          ],
          "type": "tablerow",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "$150+",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "format": 0,
                      "text": "Combine a data-heavy tool like Semrush or Ahrefs with Rext AI for content production and publishing, giving you both research depth and execution speed.",
                      "type": "text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "headerState": 0,
              "type": "tablecell",
            },
          ],
          "type": "tablerow",
        },
      ],
      "type": "table",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "If you're a solo founder or a two-person marketing team, the honest recommendation is to start with Rext AI's free tools immediately. Run a few of your existing blog posts through the Readability Checker and Keyword Density Checker, generate a sitemap and schema markup for your site, and see the kind of output quality you're working with before spending anything. From there, upgrading to the paid platform for full article generation and one-click publishing is a natural next step rather than a leap of faith.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "AI SEO Tools vs. Traditional SEO: What Actually Changed",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Traditional SEO required manually researching keywords in spreadsheets, writing content by hand, and often waiting weeks for an agency to deliver a single optimized page. AI SEO tools compress that timeline dramatically by automating the research and drafting stages, while still leaving room for human judgment on strategy, brand voice, and final review.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "altText": "Rext AI SEO content creation platform with keyword research, AI writing, SEO optimization, high-quality content, and publishing tools  ",
          "src": "https://juvrqxhye2tzsl8t.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/rext-ai-kQbU2MpOqmt9j6qVn9ok4TT1yNV0wb.png",
          "type": "image",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "It's worth being clear about what hasn't changed: keyword stuffing, thin content, and ignoring search intent still hurt rankings regardless of whether a human or an AI tool produced the page. The tools that succeed long-term, including Rext AI, are the ones built around ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "format": 0,
              "text": "E-E-A-T principles",
              "type": "text",
            },
          ],
          "title": null,
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://rext.ai/features/eeat-optimization",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " and genuine topical depth rather than just fast output. Speed without quality still fails in search results, AI-assisted or not.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "AI SEO and Answer Engine Visibility (GEO)",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "A newer consideration for small businesses is visibility inside AI-generated answers, not just traditional blue-link search results. When someone asks ChatGPT, Gemini, or Perplexity a question relevant to your business, does your content have a chance of being the source that answer draws from?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "This is where E-E-A-T optimization and sourced, citation-backed content; both built into Rext AI's content generation process; matter beyond traditional Google rankings. Content that includes clear factual statements, credible references, and well-structured comparisons is more likely to be pulled into an AI-generated answer than vague, unsupported marketing copy. For a small business, this is quickly becoming as important as ranking on page one of Google itself.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Frequently Asked Questions",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What is the best AI SEO tool for a small business with no SEO experience?",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " Rext AI is built specifically to minimize the learning curve, since it handles keyword research, writing, optimization, and publishing in one guided workflow rather than requiring you to piece together multiple specialized tools.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "How much should a small business budget for AI SEO tools?",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " Most small businesses can get meaningful results starting between $0 and $50 a month using free tools plus one focused paid platform, scaling up to $100–150 a month once content production becomes a consistent priority.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Can AI SEO tools completely replace hiring an SEO specialist?",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " For most small businesses, yes, particularly for content creation, on-page optimization, and technical basics. Highly competitive industries or complex technical SEO issues may still benefit from occasional expert input, but day-to-day execution is well within what modern AI SEO platforms handle.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What's the difference between an AI SEO tool and an AI SEO agent?",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " An AI SEO tool typically assists with one part of the process, like content scoring or keyword research. An AI SEO agent or full-workflow platform, like Rext AI, handles the entire pipeline from research through publishing with minimal manual intervention.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What should a small business look for in an AI SEO tool?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Look for features that directly support your workflow, including ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "keyword research, search-intent analysis, competitor research, content creation, on-page SEO, E-E-A-T optimization, internal linking, and publishing",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": ". Ease of use and predictable pricing are also important when SEO is handled by a small team.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Can AI SEO tools help businesses appear in ChatGPT and other AI search engines?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "AI SEO tools can help businesses create and optimize content for greater search visibility, but no tool can guarantee that a business will be mentioned by ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, or another AI system. AI-search visibility also depends on the quality and consistency of the information available across a business's website and other relevant sources.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What is the difference between an AI SEO tool and an AI writing tool?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "An AI writing tool primarily focuses on generating or editing text. An ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "AI SEO tool",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " connects content creation with SEO activities such as keyword research, search intent, SERP analysis, content optimization, and other search-focused workflows. For businesses, that distinction matters because producing text alone does not create a complete SEO strategy.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Is an all-in-one AI SEO platform useful for a small marketing team?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "It can be useful when the team needs to manage multiple SEO tasks but does not want to maintain numerous specialized subscriptions. An all-in-one workflow can reduce tool switching and make it easier to maintain a repeatable process for researching keywords, creating content, optimizing pages, and publishing them.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Final Recommendation",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "If you're a small business trying to build organic traffic without hiring a full team, start with the ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "format": 0,
              "text": "free tools",
              "type": "text",
            },
          ],
          "title": null,
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://rext.ai/tools",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " to handle immediate technical and content fixes at zero cost. Once you're ready to scale content production, Rext AI's full platform is the most complete option on this list for small teams specifically, because it replaces four or five separate subscriptions with one predictable, flat-rate tool that researches, writes, optimizes, and publishes content without you needing to become an SEO expert first.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "For businesses that specifically need deep backlink or competitor data alongside content production, pairing Rext AI with Semrush or Ahrefs gives you the best of both categories. But for most small businesses just trying to get consistent, search-optimized content published without burning out their team, Rext AI is the tool built for exactly that job.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
  ],
  "type": "root",
}
`;

exports[`blog-post-that-gets-ranked.md round-trips the same on every Lexical version: html 1`] = `"<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">How to Write a Blog Post That Gets Ranked and Remembered</span></h1><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Ever open a blank document, type a title, stare at it for ten minutes, and close the tab? You're not alone because nearly every blogger hits that wall at some point. You know you have something worth saying. You just don't know how to turn it into a post that people find, read, and remember.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">So what separates a blog post that sits at zero views from one that keeps bringing in organic traffic a year later? It's rarely writing talent. It's whether the post is built around what someone is genuinely searching for, structured for how people read online, and finished with the technical details that both Google and human attention spans reward.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This guide covers both sides. First, the fundamentals of writing a blog post that works: how to create a blog post from idea to publish, what a solid blog post structure looks like, and the blog writing tips that separate readable content from filler. Then, a full walkthrough of how Rext AI handles the same process, from research and drafting through optimization and publishing, in one connected workflow instead of six disconnected tools.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Why Do Most Blog Posts Never Get Read?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Writing usually isn't the problem, but most people can put together clear, readable sentences. What sinks a blog post before it goes live is a handful of decisions nobody made.</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Nobody checked whether anyone is actually searching for the topic.</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Nobody matched the content format to what the searcher wants.</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Nobody structured the post so it can be scanned instead of read as a wall of text.</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Nobody covered the technical SEO basics before hitting publish.</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A blog post without keyword research is a guess dressed up as content. A post without a planned blog post structure reads like a diary entry. And a post that skips on-page optimization, including the title tag, meta description, headings, and image alt text, gets buried no matter how good the sentences are.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Blog post writing, done properly, was never just writing. It's research, structure, optimization, and distribution. Most guides only teach the first one.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">What Actually Makes a Blog Post Work?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Before you open any tool, answer the six questions below. If you can't answer one yet, that's where to start.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">1. Who is this for?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Your target audience should be clear enough that you could describe one real reader because a &nbsp;post that tries to speak to everyone usually speaks to no one.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">2. What does the searcher want when they type this query?</strong></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;This is search intent, sometimes called reader intent, and it's the most overlooked factor in blog writing. Someone searching "how to write a copywriting post" wants steps, and someone searching "best copywriting and blogging platforms" wants a comparison. If the format and the intent don't match, good writing won't rescue the page.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">3. Can someone scan the structure in ten seconds?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">You need a single H1, a clean hierarchy of H2s and H3s, and short paragraphs. If a reader can't tell what the post covers from the headings alone, the structure needs work.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">4. Is there proof you know the subject?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Search engines evaluate this as E-E-A-T: experience, expertise, authoritativeness, and trustworthiness. Specific detail, real sourcing, and a credible voice beat generic advice every time.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">5. Have you checked the technical basics?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Title tag length, meta description, image alt text, heading order. They feel unglamorous, but they often decide whether a page lands on page one or nowhere.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">6. What happens after someone finishes reading?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Every post needs a reason for the reader to do something next, whether that's subscribing, clicking through to a related article, or leaving a comment.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Keep these six questions close. Everything else here exists to help you answer them faster.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"><span style="display: inline-block;" data-lexical-decorator="true"></span><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">So How Does an AI platform actually speed up the blog writing process?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Many people are skeptical here, and fairly so. Plenty of "AI blog writers" generate generic text and stop, leaving you to handle the research, optimization, and publishing on your own. Rext AI takes a different route. The whole pipeline, from your first keyword to a published article, sits inside one connected workflow. If you are new, read the </span><a href="https://rext.ai/get-started" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">Let’s Start guide</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> for account creation and concise steps. Here is how it runs.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 1: Set up your workspace</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Once you're inside the platform, you create a workspace by entering a name and your website URL. That one step does more than it looks like. Rext AI scrapes your site and runs it through a short analysis pipeline with five stages: Website Scraping, Brand Voice Extraction, Competitor Analysis, Persona Extraction, and Finalization.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">When it finishes, the platform already understands your brand's tone, who your competitors are, and who your target reader is, without you typing a single instruction. You can review and adjust anything it found before moving on, but most of the groundwork that would take a human researcher an afternoon is already done.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 2: Start a project and enter your keyword</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">From the dashboard, click "Start Fresh," then "Begin Research," and enter the keyword or topic you want the post built around.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Not sure what to type? That's common, and it's worth solving before you commit. Free tools help here. Before you open the main platform, run your rough idea through a topic generator or content idea generator to get a sharper starting point than a vague one.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 3: Let it research the keyword</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Submit your keyword, and Rext AI runs a multi-stage research process in the background. It creates the session, normalizes search results, extracts competitor data, pulls SERP information, and analyzes backlink metrics. What comes back is keyword intent, search volume, and a difficulty score, the same data a human researcher would spend twenty or thirty minutes assembling by hand.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 4: Review the keyword suggestions</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Alongside your original keyword, Rext AI shows related keyword opportunities from the same research pass. You can stay with your original term or switch to a stronger related one, depending on your goals.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 5: Choose the right content type</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Does your topic need to be a blog post, or would it work better as a how-to guide, a checklist, or a comparison? Most writers never ask, and it costs them rankings.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Rext AI shows a grid of content formats: Blog, How-To Guide, Explainer, Pillar Content, Checklist, Tutorial, FAQ, White Paper, and Case Study. Each is matched to your keyword's search intent, and one is flagged as "Recommended." A how-to search wants numbered steps. A comparison search wants criteria side by side. Getting the format right is half the ranking battle, and it happens before a single sentence is written.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"><span style="display: inline-block;" data-lexical-decorator="true"></span><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 6: Pick your title</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Next, the platform generates several title and angle options tagged by content pillar and intent, with one marked "Recommended." You can pick one, regenerate the set, or type your own direction if none fit. If you're unsure which title has the best chance of earning a click, test it rather than guess. A free headline scoring tool is useful before you lock anything in.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 7: Review and approve the outline</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This is where the platform's depth shows, and it's what separates it from a basic AI writer. Before generating any body content, Rext AI builds a full content brief that includes:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Tone and audience, both editable directly.</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A focus keyphrase, plus a target word count and content schema.</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A tag list of supporting keywords to include naturally throughout.</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword clusters, meaning groups of related terms organized by intent, so you can see which subtopics the article covers and why they matter.</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A section-by-section structure with bullet points describing what each part will say.</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A suggested author persona matched to the topic and search intent for E-E-A-T credibility, which you can swap or remove.</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A brand promotion block, where the platform suggests a natural, contextual mention of your business, with a relevance match score and a simple toggle to include or exclude it.</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If something's off, you're not stuck with it. Type your feedback into the regenerate box and the outline rebuilds around your notes before you approve it.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 8: Watch it generate</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">After you approve the outline, the writing runs through a visible three-stage pipeline. Generating Content works from the approved outline. Humanizing smooths tone and phrasing so the piece doesn't read like obvious AI output. Reviewing Content is a final internal quality pass. A full-length article typically takes a couple of minutes here, not hours.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 9: Edit inside the built-in editor</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This may be the most underrated part of the workflow. You land in a three-panel editor. On the left is a clickable outline so you can jump to any section. In the center is the article with a full rich-text toolbar covering headings, bold, italic, lists, quotes, links, tables, and images. On the right is a live "Performance &amp; SEO" score out of 100, with a running checklist for title length, meta description length, mobile configuration, heading hierarchy, content length, text-to-HTML ratio, image alt text coverage, and Open Graph tags.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Make an edit and watch the score respond. You're never guessing whether a change helped or hurt.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Step 10: Export or publish</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">When you're happy with the piece, two sets of options sit in the top corner. You can export as HTML, Markdown, or plain text, or publish directly: Publish live, Save as Draft, Submit for Review, or Schedule for Later. If your WordPress site is connected, publishing sends the article straight to your CMS. There's no copy-pasting, no reformatting, and no re-uploading images by hand. Scheduled posting also makes it easier to keep a steady publishing schedule without logging in every time a post is due.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Do I Still Need Separate SEO Tools If I'm Using All This?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Fair question. The honest answer depends on which side of "publish" you're standing on.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Before you publish</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Even a fully AI-generated draft benefits from a few checks that a content generator alone won't always flag.</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Is your title the strongest option, or just the first one you liked?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/headline-analyzer" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">A headline analyzer</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> powered by Rext AI settles it in seconds.</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Does the draft read naturally at your audience's level?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Rext AI’s </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/readability-checker" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">readability checker</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> shows where you land on the Flesch-Kincaid scale, so you're not relying on gut feeling.</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Will your meta description get clicked in a crowded results page?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> A meta description generator handles it in one pass.</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Does your keyword usage read naturally?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> A quick </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/keyword-density-checker" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">keyword density check</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> by the Rext AI density checker tool tells you whether it drifted toward stuffing before Google's quality systems notice.</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">These aren't optional extras. They're the last line of defense between a solid draft and one with a small, avoidable flaw that quietly caps its performance.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">After you publish</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This is the part almost every beginner's guide skips, because getting a post live is only half the job.</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Will the new URL get crawled and indexed promptly?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> That depends on a current sitemap and a robots.txt file that isn't accidentally blocking the section you just published in.</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Is the post eligible for rich results?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Star ratings and FAQ dropdowns can lift click-through rate, and they depend on proper schema markup, which most writers never think to check.</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Is anything on your site leaking SEO value through dead links?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> A </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/broken-link-checker" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">broken link checker</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> catches that before it turns into a slow, invisible drag on your rankings.</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">How will the listing look in Google's results?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> A </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/serp-preview" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">SERP preview tool</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> lets you see it before it goes live instead of after.</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The pattern is simple. Writing the post is one job. Making sure it's technically sound before publishing, and properly set up to be found afterward, are two more. They quietly decide whether all that writing effort pays off. Rext AI's free tools at rext.ai/tools cover this before-and-after gap with no account required, so they're worth bookmarking regardless of which platform you use to write the post itself.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Getting the Post Seen: Content Distribution After Publishing</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A published post isn't a finished post. Even well-optimized content needs a push in its first weeks, especially on a newer site. A few habits make a real difference:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Share it on social media</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> in a format that fits each platform, not the same link pasted everywhere. A short takeaway or a strong stat works better than "new post is live."</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Send it to your email newsletter.</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Subscribers already trust you, and early clicks and engagement give a new page momentum.</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Add internal links</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> from older, related posts to the new one, and link forward from the new post to your best existing content. It helps readers move through your site and helps search engines understand how your topics connect.</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Reply to comments.</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Audience engagement builds a small community around your blog, and a real conversation under a post tells readers there's a person behind it.</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Keep a publishing schedule you can sustain.</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Weekly or twice a month is fine. Consistency builds more long-term authority than a burst of posts followed by months of silence.</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Blog content creation doesn't end at the publish button. The posts that keep bringing in organic traffic are usually the ones someone kept promoting, updating, and linking to.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">What If You're Not Ready to Commit to a Full Platform Yet?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That's a reasonable place to be, and you don't need a paid tool to start writing better posts today. Open the free tools page and run your next post idea through the </span><a href="https://rext.ai/tools/topic-generator" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">topic generator</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> to sharpen the angle. Build a quick outline with the content outline generator. Once you've drafted something, check it with the readability checker and grammar checker before you publish. Each step is free, takes under a minute, and answers one of the six questions from earlier in this guide.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">How Does This Compare to Just Using a Chatbot?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">It's a natural instinct: why not ask ChatGPT to write the post? A general-purpose chatbot can write, but writing was never the whole job. It doesn't know your keyword's search volume or difficulty unless you tell it. It doesn't know what your competitors already cover unless you paste it in. It doesn't know your brand voice unless you re-explain it every session. And once it finishes, you're still checking on-page SEO by hand, formatting for your CMS, and copying everything into WordPress.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><a href="https://rext.ai/" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">Rext AI</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true">'s advantage isn't that the writing is dramatically different. It's that the research, brand consistency, SEO scoring, and publishing are already built into one workflow, so you're not stitching together five tools and re-explaining your business to each one.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Conclusion:</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Writing a blog post that performs was never about stringing together good sentences. It's research, structure, optimization, and distribution: four jobs that most people try to squeeze into one sitting with no system behind them. Whether you handle each piece by hand or use a connected workflow like Rext AI, from automatic brand analysis and keyword research through outline approval, generation, on-page scoring, and direct publishing, the fundamentals at the start of this guide stay the same.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Frequently Asked Questions</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">How do you write a blog post from scratch?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Start with your target audience and a clear goal, then pick a topic through keyword research. Check what already ranks on Google, build an outline with headings and subheadings, and write the introduction, body, and conclusion in that order. Finish with the title tag, meta description, internal links, and formatting before you publish. The steps in the blog writing process section above cover each stage.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">How long should a blog post be?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> There's no universal number, and anyone quoting a fixed word count without knowing your topic is guessing. Search intent decides. A quick, specific answer may need only 700 to 1,000 words, while a competitive, broad topic often needs well over 2,000. The real test is whether you've said everything the reader needs, no more and no less.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">**How do I come up with blog post ideas when I'm stuck?**Think back to a question you had when you were new to your niche, then write the answer you wish someone had given you. Beyond that, "People Also Ask" boxes, related searches, and questions from online communities will give you more topic ideas than you can use. A topic generator or content idea generator can speed that up.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Do I need to understand SEO to write a good blog post?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> You don't need to become a technical expert, but you should know the basics: what your reader is searching for, how to organize headings, and why meta descriptions and alt text matter. You can learn as you go, or lean on tools that handle the technical layer while you focus on the writing.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Will an AI-written blog post rank, or does Google penalize AI content?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Search engines look at whether content is genuinely helpful and shows real expertise, not whether a person or a program wrote the first draft. Generic, shallow output struggles no matter who produced it. Content built on real keyword research, matched to the right format, and refined with a humanization pass has as much chance to rank as anything written by hand.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">How often should I publish new blog posts?</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Consistency matters more than frequency. A rhythm you can maintain, whether weekly or twice a month, builds more authority than an intense burst followed by silence.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold"