          ],
          "type": "listitem",
          "value": 4,
        },
      ],
      "listType": "bullet",
      "tag": "ul",
      "type": "list",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "4. ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Core SEO Capabilities Are Unlimited Across Paid Plans.",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": " Rext states that these core SEO features remain available across all paid plans.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "5. ",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Pricing Is Based on Credits",
          "type": "text",
        },
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": ", Not Vague Word Limits",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "format": 0,
              "text": "  Credits apply to content-generation actions.",
              "type": "text",
            },
          ],
          "type": "listitem",
          "value": 1,
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "format": 0,
              "text": "  Core SEO research and optimization features remain available across plans.",
              "type": "text",
            },
          ],
          "type": "listitem",
          "value": 2,
        },
      ],
      "listType": "bullet",
      "tag": "ul",
      "type": "list",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Rext AI Covers SEO Beyond Content Generation With Free SEO Tools",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h2",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "One of the biggest differences in the Rext AI approach is that SEO does not stop when the article is generated. Rext also provides a collection of free SEO tools that can be used independently for individual optimization tasks. ",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Its current free-tool ecosystem includes tools such as a SERP Preview, Word Counter, Paragraph Rewriter, Keyword Density Checker, Sitemap Generator, Robots.txt Generator, Canonical Tag Generator, Hreflang Tag Generator, Schema Markup Generator, Content Outline Generator, Headline Analyzer, Meta Description Generator, and other SEO-focused utilities.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "This matters because not every SEO task requires an AI content subscription. Sometimes you already have an article and only need to check keyword usage. Sometimes you need to preview a title and meta description, generate schema markup, create a sitemap, prepare robots.txt, or rewrite one paragraph for clarity. Rext's free tools allow those individual tasks to be handled without requiring users to build a separate collection of small SEO utilities.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Rext AI vs Jasper for SEO: The Key Difference",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h2",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Jasper absolutely supports SEO. Its official SEO offering includes SEO-focused agents, content optimization, keyword and competitor research, and integrations with tools such as Semrush and Surfer SEO. Jasper also positions its platform around SEO, AEO, and GEO, showing that search optimization is now an important part of its broader marketing platform.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Rext AI takes a more concentrated approach. SEO is built into the product from keyword discovery through content production and on-page optimization, while its free SEO tools extend that workflow to standalone tasks. Its keyword research system includes search volume, keyword difficulty, intent classification, competitor gap analysis, related keyword groups, long-tail opportunities, and topical authority mapping.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "The same SEO-first approach continues after writing. Rext's on-page SEO capabilities cover semantic heading structures, internal linking, image alt text, feature-snippet formatting, and schema markup. Its technical SEO tool collection also includes sitemap, robots.txt, canonical, hreflang, and SERP preview tools.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "That makes Rext useful for two different situations. If you are creating new content, you can use its full SEO workflow from keyword research to article generation and optimization. If you already have content, you can use its free SEO tools to handle specific optimization jobs without rebuilding the entire article. Rext itself describes these free tools as standalone pieces of the same SEO logic used inside its broader content workflow.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "For SEO agencies, niche-site owners, publishers, and marketers, this creates a practical advantage: the platform is not asking you to choose between "AI writing" and "SEO software." It brings the two closer together. Rext AI's value is that SEO is not an extra layer added after writing; it is part of the workflow that determines what gets researched, written, optimized, and published in the first place.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Why This Makes Rext AI More Than a Low-Cost Jasper Alternative",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h2",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Calling Rext AI simply a cheaper Jasper alternative misses the more important distinction. Rext is built around a different center of gravity: SEO content operations. Its pricing makes the platform accessible starting at $32/month, but its feature set goes beyond basic article generation with keyword research, SERP analysis, E-E-A-T, on-page SEO, content planning, humanization, and publishing workflows.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "In other words, the argument for Rext AI is not that it costs less because it does less. The stronger argument is that teams focused on organic search can get a focused SEO workflow without paying for a broader marketing platform simply to access the content capabilities they use most. For teams that need extensive marketing governance, audiences, brand intelligence, and campaign workflows, Jasper's broader platform remains relevant. For teams where SEO content is the center of the operation, Rext AI puts those SEO capabilities much closer to the core.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "And because Rext also maintains a library of free SEO tools, users can access practical optimization utilities even when they do not need the full AI content workflow. That makes the Rext ecosystem useful not only for generating new articles, but also for improving, checking, and preparing existing content for search.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "How Rext AI Fits a Modern Content Workflow",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h2",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "A practical SEO workflow usually begins with a question or topic, not with an empty document. You identify the search opportunity, examine intent, evaluate the competition, collect related concepts, plan the article, produce the draft, review the claims, optimize the content, and publish it. The closer a platform can bring these steps together, the fewer manual handoffs your team has to manage.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Rext AI is designed around this type of process. Its current product materials describe deep keyword analysis, one-click article generation, E-E-A-T optimization, agency workspaces, bulk generation, and publishing. Its help center also documents a workflow that begins with keyword input and analysis before moving through article type and outline approval.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "That can be particularly useful for agencies and publishers. When the same process needs to be repeated across many websites, reducing repetitive research and formatting work can free editors to spend more time on the parts AI cannot replace: reviewing facts, adding genuine experience, improving examples, checking sources, and deciding whether the article is actually useful.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "The goal should not be to remove humans from content production. A better goal is to remove unnecessary manual work so humans can spend more time making the content accurate, distinctive, and valuable.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Frequently Asked Questions About Jasper vs Rext AI",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h2",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What is the main difference between Jasper and Rext AI?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "The main difference is their product emphasis. Jasper is currently positioned as a broad AI platform for marketing teams, with agents, content pipelines, brand intelligence, knowledge, audiences, and AI discovery capabilities. Rext AI focuses more specifically on SEO content operations, including keyword research, search intent, topical clustering, article generation, E-E-A-T optimization, and publishing.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Is Rext AI a Jasper AI alternative for SEO content?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Rext AI can be considered an alternative for teams whose primary requirement is SEO-focused content production. Its current workflow includes keyword analysis, intent classification, competitor gap analysis, topic clusters, structured article generation, and E-E-A-T-oriented content features. Whether it is the right alternative depends on the rest of your workflow, especially if you also need extensive marketing governance or campaign management.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Which platform is more focused on keyword research?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Rext AI places keyword research directly at the center of its SEO workflow. Its official keyword research documentation includes search volume, difficulty, intent classification, keyword gap analysis, long-tail opportunities, related keyword grouping, and topical authority mapping. Jasper also provides research capabilities, but its broader platform is designed around marketing execution rather than only SEO research.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What should I consider when choosing between Jasper alternatives?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Look at the complete workflow instead of comparing isolated AI-writing features. Consider whether you need brand voice management, enterprise knowledge, campaign workflows, keyword research, search intent analysis, topical clustering, long-form article generation, E-E-A-T support, collaboration, integrations, and publishing. The best fit depends on which of those activities your team performs most often and where your existing process creates the most manual work.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What are the best Jasper AI alternatives for SEO content?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "The right alternative depends on whether you need SEO research, blog writing, content optimization, or a broader marketing workflow. User discussions show users looking for alternatives mainly because of Jasper's cost, SEO content needs, or a desire for a simpler writing experience, and you can opt for Rext AI for your content needs.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "Is there a more affordable alternative to Jasper for SEO writing?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Yes, several AI writing platforms like Rext AI are positioned as lower-cost alternatives, but pricing and features vary. One recent SEO discussion specifically raised concerns about Jasper's subscription cost and asked for a more cost-effective option for SEO content.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What is a good Jasper alternative for writing blog posts?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "For blog writing, look for a platform that can handle more than basic text generation, like Rext AI. Useful capabilities include content outlines, long-form writing, SEO research, search intent analysis, optimization, and editing, especially if the articles are intended to attract organic traffic. All of the discussed features are included in Rext AI with affordable cost options.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 1,
          "text": "What is the best Jasper alternative for agencies producing SEO content?",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "tag": "h3",
      "type": "heading",
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "format": 0,
          "text": "Agencies should compare platforms based on bulk production, keyword research, client workspaces, brand controls, collaboration, optimization, and publishing workflows. The best fit will depend on how many clients you manage and how much of the SEO process you want to keep inside one platform. Rext AI provides an SEO-centered approach, connecting keyword research, search intent, topical analysis, content generation, E-E-A-T-oriented optimization, and bulk publishing for agencies at affordable prices.",
          "type": "text",
        },
      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
  ],
  "type": "root",
}
`;

exports[`surfer-seo-alternatives.md round-trips the same on every Lexical version: html 1`] = `"<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">8 Best Surfer SEO Alternatives for Content Optimization</span></h1><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">&nbsp;If you are comparing Surfer SEO alternatives, focus on more than a content score. The strongest choice should fit your full workflow, including SERP research, keyword analysis, content briefs, writing, optimization, publishing, and increasingly, visibility across AI search.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Surfer remains a capable content optimization platform; however, different teams need different things. Some want lower pricing. Others need deeper content strategy, stronger keyword research, automated publishing, AI writing, or tools built around Google and generative search together.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This guide compares nine options and related platforms based on what they actually help you accomplish, rather than treating every SEO tool as interchangeable.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">1. Why Look for a Surfer SEO Alternative?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Surfer SEO helps writers and SEO teams create content based on what already performs in search. Its platform includes content optimization, keyword research, auditing, AI writing, and AI visibility features. New accounts can currently test its Pro plan through a seven-day trial; the core idea is useful. Enter a target query, study the SERPs, identify relevant terms and topics, then improve your page against those signals.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">So why switch?</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Usually, the problem is not that Surfer cannot optimize content. The issue is that different businesses have different workflows, so you may want an alternative to Surfer SEO if you need:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Lower monthly costs</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  More articles within your budget</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Built-in keyword research</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Stronger content planning</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI-assisted drafting</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Automated CMS publishing</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Better agency workflows</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  More flexible team access</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI search monitoring</span></li><li value="10" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A different approach to content scoring</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">There is another practical reason that a high optimization score does not automatically make a page useful or rankable.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content still needs to satisfy search intent, show real expertise, answer the query clearly, and offer something that competing pages do not. Google does not rank a page simply because an SEO content editor gives it a high score.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This is a common mistake when teams first adopt content optimization software. Writers start chasing every recommended phrase instead of asking whether the extra text helps the reader.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Treat optimization scores as guidance, not a finish line.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">2. What Should You Look for in the Best Surfer SEO Alternatives?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The best Surfer alternatives should solve a real weakness in your current workflow.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Before comparing prices, write down what you actually need the software to do. This prevents you from paying for a large platform when you only use two features.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">SERP analysis</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A useful SERP analysis tool should help you understand the pages competing for your query.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Look beyond word counts. You want information that helps answer questions such as:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  What topics appear repeatedly?</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  What does the searcher expect?</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Which competitors should you compare against?</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Which subtopics are missing?</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  How comprehensive does the page need to be?</span></li></ul><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Content scoring</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A content scoring tool gives writers a measurable optimization target that can make editing faster, especially across a large content team. But the score should support editorial judgment rather than replace it.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A page can hit an excellent score and still be weak if it lacks original insight, uses awkward keywords, or fails to answer the searcher's main question.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Keyword research and clustering</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Some platforms focus mainly on individual articles, and others combine content optimization with keyword research, keyword clustering, and topic discovery.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The second approach may make more sense when you are building topical authority rather than optimizing one page at a time.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">AI writing</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">AI writing can reduce production time, but volume alone has little value.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Look at what happens before and after generations. Does the software research the topic? Can it build a useful outline? Does it support your brand voice? Can you review SEO recommendations before publishing?</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A good workflow should make human review easier, not encourage blind publishing.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Content briefs</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Agencies and editorial teams should pay close attention to content briefs.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A useful content brief gives a writer direction before the first sentence gets written. It may cover search intent, headings, competing pages, important topics, questions, keywords, and other requirements.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That saves editors from fixing strategic problems after a 2,000-word draft already exists.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">AI search visibility</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Traditional Google rankings are no longer the only discovery surface worth watching.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content may also appear or receive citations in Google AI Overviews and platforms such as ChatGPT and other AI search experiences.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Do not assume that an "AI optimized" label guarantees citations. No SEO optimization software can guarantee that an AI system will cite a particular page.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Instead, look for tools that help you create clear, well-structured, well-sourced content and measure visibility where relevant.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Workflow and integrations</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Finally, consider what happens after optimization.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If your team writes in Google Docs, works inside WordPress, manages Shopify sites, or depends on Google Search Console, integrations can save significant time.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The best software is often the one people actually use consistently.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"><span style="display: inline-block;" data-lexical-decorator="true"></span><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">3. Rext AI, An AI-Focused Alternative to Surfer SEO</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><a href="https://rext.ai/" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">Rext AI</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> takes a broader approach to the SEO content workflow. Instead of stopping at recommendations inside a content editor, it combines keyword research, SERP analysis, outline generation, article generation, EEAT analysis, on-page SEO, humanization, and optional CMS publishing within one workflow.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That makes it worth considering when your main problem is not simply optimizing an existing draft. It is more relevant when you want to reduce the number of separate steps needed to move from a keyword to a publishable article.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its current feature set includes:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Unlimited keyword research across paid plans</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Analysis of the top 10 SERP results</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  EEAT injection and analysis</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  On-page SEO optimization</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Outline and article generation</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  A humanization pass</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Optional AI image generation</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  CMS publishing, including WordPress</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Multiple workspaces on higher plans</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A useful distinction is the credit system. The company publishes the credit cost for individual actions instead of describing usage only through vague word limits. A standard SEO article is listed at 15 credits, while optional actions can use additional credits.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For teams producing content at scale, that makes monthly output easier to estimate.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Current monthly </span><a href="https://rext.ai/pricing" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">pricing</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> starts at:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Starter:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $39 per month, 400 credits</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Growth:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $89 per month, 1,000 credits</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pro:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $189 per month, 2,400 credits</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Agency:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $399 per month, 5,500 credits</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Annual billing currently reduces paid plan pricing by 20%. The platform also offers a free trial without requiring a card to start.&nbsp;</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This approach makes the most sense for marketers, publishers, bloggers, and agencies that want research, generation, optimization, and publishing closer together.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">It may be less relevant if you already have a mature writing stack and only want a dedicated optimization editor.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">4. Clearscope, A Surfer SEO Competitor for Content Optimization</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Clearscope is a well-established option for teams that care heavily about content quality, optimization, and structured editorial workflows.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its current offering has also expanded beyond traditional SEO. Clearscope now describes its plans around both SEO and AI search visibility, with tracked prompts and pages included in its packages.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That makes the platform particularly interesting for established content teams that want to monitor content rather than optimize a draft once and forget about it.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Clearscope focuses on areas such as:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content optimization</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Topic exploration</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content drafts</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Page tracking</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI search visibility</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Prompt tracking</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Unlimited users</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Unlimited projects</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">One benefit for larger editorial teams is its unlimited user model. You do not necessarily want pricing to jump every time another editor, strategist, or writer needs access.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Clearscope currently lists three primary plans:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Essentials:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $129 per month</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Business:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $399 per month</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Enterprise:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> Custom pricing</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Essentials currently includes 50 tracked prompts, 50 pages, 20 monthly Topic Explorations, and 20 monthly Drafts. Business increases the tracked prompts and pages to 300 each and adds a dedicated account manager. A 14-day free trial is available.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That places Clearscope toward the premium end of this comparison.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Clearscope is worth considering for editorial and content teams that place a high value on optimization quality and do not need the cheapest possible platform.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If budget is your biggest constraint, lower-priced alternatives may make more sense.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"><span style="display: inline-block;" data-lexical-decorator="true"></span><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">5. Frase, A Surfer SEO Alternative for SERP Research and AI Writing</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Frase has evolved from an SEO research and optimization product into what it calls a content operating system for AI search.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its current workflow combines content creation with SEO and GEO scoring, publishing, auditing, and AI visibility features. The Starter plan can publish directly to WordPress, Webflow, Sanity, Wix, or FraseCMS.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That combination makes Frase attractive when research and writing need to happen in the same environment.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Depending on the plan, Frase can support:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SEO and GEO scoring</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content research</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content optimization</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI-assisted writing</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content auditing</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI visibility monitoring</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  CMS publishing</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content decay monitoring</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The practical advantage is workflow continuity. Research does not have to live in one platform, the brief in another, and publishing somewhere else.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That can matter more than having the longest feature list.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Frase currently lists its Starter plan at $49 per month when billed monthly, or $39 per month with annual billing. It includes one seat, one site, 10 articles, and 50 audit pages per month. A seven-day trial is available without a credit card.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Higher plans increase capacity and are aimed at content teams with larger workflows.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Frase fits writers and teams that want SERP research, optimization, drafting, and publishing connected in one workflow.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">It is also worth exploring if GEO scoring and AI visibility are becoming part of your content process.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">6. MarketMuse, A Surfer SEO Alternative for Content Strategy</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse approaches SEO from a different angle.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">While individual page optimization matters, MarketMuse places substantial emphasis on your broader content inventory, topical coverage, gaps, and content strategy.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This distinction becomes important when a site already has hundreds or thousands of pages.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">At that point, asking "How should we optimize this article?" is only part of the problem.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">You also need to ask:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Which topic should we cover next?</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Where is our authority strongest?</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Which existing page deserves an update?</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  What are we missing?</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Which content opportunity deserves resources?</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse is designed around those larger content decisions.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its current platform includes:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Topic Navigator</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword research</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SERP X ray</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SERP Heatmap</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Site Heatmap</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content inventories</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Tracked topics</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content briefs</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Strategy documents</span></li><li value="10" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content optimization</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse says it uses proprietary data and topic modeling rather than relying only on generic API data.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse currently offers:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Free:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> 10 queries per month</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Optimize:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> includes 100 tracked topics and five briefs monthly</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Research:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> includes 1,000 tracked topics and 10 briefs</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Strategy:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> includes 10,000 tracked topics and 20 briefs</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its public pricing page currently directs users to book a demo for paid tiers rather than displaying dollar prices in the retrieved plan summary.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The free level is notable because users searching for a Surfer SEO free alternative can explore parts of the platform before moving into a paid workflow.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse is best suited to content strategists, established publishers, and larger teams that need to decide what to create and update across an entire content library.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If you only need a simple editor for one article at a time, it may be more platform than you need.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">7. NeuronWriter, An Affordable Surfer SEO Alternative</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">NeuronWriter stands out mainly because it offers a wide range of SEO and AI features at comparatively accessible starting prices.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its platform combines content optimization with AI writing, content planning, integrations, plagiarism checks on qualifying plans, and AI visibility monitoring.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That makes it one of the more interesting affordable Surfer SEO alternatives for small teams.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Depending on your plan, features include:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content Writer analyses</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI writing credits</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content planning</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI templates</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content Designer</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Plagiarism checks</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Google Search Console integration</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  WordPress integration</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Shopify integration</span></li><li value="10" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  API access on qualifying plans</span></li><li value="11" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI monitored questions</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">NeuronWriter also lists monitoring across Google, Google AI Overviews, AI Mode, ChatGPT, and Perplexity through its AI Monitoring offering.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Current monthly prices are:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Bronze:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $23</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Silver:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $45</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Gold:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $69</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Platinum:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $93</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Diamond:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> $117</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Annual billing reduces those monthly equivalent prices to $19, $37, $57, $77, and $97 respectively. A seven day trial under Gold plan terms is available.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The Gold plan is where several advanced capabilities become available, including integrations, advanced AI templates, plagiarism checking, and Content Designer.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">NeuronWriter deserves consideration from freelancers, bloggers, small agencies, and site owners who want NLP SEO tools and content optimization without starting at a high monthly price.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">When comparing Surfer SEO vs NeuronWriter, pay close attention to limits and workflow rather than price alone.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"><span style="display: inline-block;" data-lexical-decorator="true"></span><img data-lexical-decorator-boundary="true" alt="" style="position: absolute !important; width: 0px !important; height: 0px !important; border: 0px !important; margin: 0px !important; padding: 0px;"></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">8. Semrush SEO Writing Assistant vs Surfer SEO</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Semrush is the broadest SEO ecosystem in this comparison.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">That makes Semrush vs Surfer SEO slightly different from comparing two dedicated content editors.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Surfer centers heavily on content optimization and related content workflows. Semrush covers a much wider SEO stack, including keyword research, competitor research, site auditing, position tracking, content tools, and more.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For content specifically, there are two offerings worth understanding.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The SEO Writing Assistant evaluates areas such as SEO, readability, tone, and originality. Semrush also offers a newer Content Toolkit for ideation, briefs, AI content creation, optimization, and publishing.&nbsp;</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The content ecosystem includes capabilities such as:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Topic discovery</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SEO brief generation</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI article creation</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content optimization</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Brand voice</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SEO recommendations</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI rewriting</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  WordPress publishing</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  SERP backed optimization</span></li><li value="10" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Broader keyword and competitor data</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The bigger advantage appears when your team already uses Semrush.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Adding content tools to an existing SEO workflow may be simpler than adopting another standalone platform.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The Semrush Content Toolkit currently costs $60 per month and offers a seven day free trial. It includes unlimited standard articles, five SEO boosted articles per month, SEO briefs, content ideas, optimization, AI rewriting, and WordPress export.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The separate SEO Toolkit currently starts at $139.95 per month for Pro, while Guru costs $249.95 and Business costs $499.95 monthly. SEO Writing Assistant is included at the Guru level according to Semrush's current plan documentation.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This distinction matters. Do not assume every Semrush content feature comes with its cheapest SEO subscription.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Semrush makes the most sense when content optimization is only one part of your SEO work.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If you also need keyword research, technical SEO, competitor analysis, and rank tracking, consolidating tools may be useful.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If you only want a focused content optimization experience, a dedicated platform may feel simpler.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">9. Content Harmony and WriterZen as Surfer SEO Competitors</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Not every Surfer SEO competitor tries to solve the same problem.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content Harmony and WriterZen illustrate this well. One places greater emphasis on structured content workflows and briefs. The other has strong keyword research and clustering functionality.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Content Harmony</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content Harmony is built around repeatable content workflows.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Each Content Workflow includes a Keyword Report, Content Brief, and Content Grader. This creates a logical process from research to instructions to final optimization.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword reports</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Search intent research</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content briefs</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content grading</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Unlimited users</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Unlimited projects</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Rollover credits</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Team training</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For agencies, unlimited users and projects can be particularly useful. A cheap base plan becomes less attractive if every additional team member creates another fee.</span></p><h4 dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h4><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Pricing scales by monthly Content Workflows:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  5 workflows: $50 per month</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  12 workflows: $99</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  25 workflows: $199</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  50 workflows: $299</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  100 workflows: $599</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  150 workflows: $799</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Enterprise: from $1,000 per month</span></li></ul><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">There is also a $10 trial that provides 10 workflow credits and does not automatically convert into a subscription.&nbsp;</span></p><h4 dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h4><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content Harmony is particularly relevant for agencies and content teams that need standardized briefs and a clear handoff between strategists, writers, and editors.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">WriterZen</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">WriterZen takes a more keyword centered approach.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">It is useful when your challenge begins before the writing stage. Instead of simply asking how to optimize one article, you can research keywords and group related opportunities before building the content.</span></p><h4 dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Key Features</strong></h4><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its current plans advertise capabilities such as:</span></p><ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword research</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword clustering</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword lists</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Keyword Explorer</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Content Creator</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  AI writing on qualifying plans</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Plagiarism checking</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Topic discovery</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true">  Team collaboration</span></li></ul><h4 dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Pricing Plans</strong></h4><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">WriterZen currently promotes one time pricing rather than a standard monthly subscription.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Its Keyword Research package is listed at $135 one time, while All In One Basic costs $270 one time. The latter adds Content Creator functionality, up to 50 articles per month, unlimited AI writing, and plagiarism checking. That pricing structure is unusual in a category dominated by subscriptions.</span></p><h4 dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Best For</strong></h4><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">WriterZen is worth considering when keyword discovery and keyword clustering are major parts of your workflow.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">It may be particularly attractive to people who dislike adding another recurring software subscription.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">10. Surfer SEO Alternatives Comparison: Features, Pricing and Best Use Cases</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">There is no single feature that determines the right platform.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Use this comparison as a starting point, then test your shortlist with the type of content you actually produce.</span></p><table class="border-collapse w-full my-4" dir="auto"><tr dir="auto"><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Tool</span></p></th><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Best For</span></p></th><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">SERP/SEO Analysis</span></p></th><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">AI Writing</span></p></th><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Broader Planning</span></p></th><th class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm font-semibold" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Starting Price</span></p></th></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Rext AI</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">End to end Complete SEO workflow</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Strong</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$32/mo</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Clearscope</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Editorial optimization</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Draft workflow</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$129/mo</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Frase</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Research, writing and GEO workflow</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$49/mo monthly</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">MarketMuse</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content strategy and topical planning</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Optimization focused</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Strong</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Free tier</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">NeuronWriter</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Affordable optimization</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$23/mo</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Semrush Content Toolkit</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Wider SEO and content workflow</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Strong</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$60/mo</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Content Harmony</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Briefs and agency workflows</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">No core focus</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Strong</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$50/mo</span></p></td></tr><tr dir="auto"><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">WriterZen</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Keyword research and clustering</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes on qualifying plan</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Strong</span></p></td><td class="border border-border px-2 py-2 !pb-0 align-top min-w-0 w-auto relative outline-none text-sm" dir="auto"><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">$135 one time</span></p></td></tr></table><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Pricing and features change, sometimes quickly. The figures above reflect publicly available pricing checked in September 2026.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">A better way to choose is to identify your bottleneck.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If writing takes too long:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> prioritize an AI SEO tool that connects research, outlining, generation, and optimization.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If writers miss search intent:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> prioritize SERP research and strong content briefs.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If your editors spend hours fixing drafts:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> prioritize clear grading and optimization guidance.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If you do not know what to publish:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> prioritize keyword research, topic discovery, clustering, and content gap analysis.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If you manage many clients:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> consider workspaces, users, API integrations, reporting, and publishing workflow.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">If you already have hundreds of articles:</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> content inventory, auditing, performance analysis, and planning become more valuable than another writing interface.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">This is also where buying based on a feature checklist can go wrong.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Imagine an agency publishes 80 articles per month. A $30 tool may sound cheaper, but not if the team spends another 20 minutes moving every article between research, writing, optimization, and WordPress.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Those 20 minutes become more than 26 hours across 80 articles.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Workflow cost matters alongside subscription cost.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">11. Which Surfer SEO Alternative Should You Choose?</strong></h2><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Start with what you want to improve.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For an </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">end to end AI content workflow</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, look for software that can move from keyword and SERP research into drafting, optimization, and publishing without unnecessary handoffs.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">editorial optimization</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, Clearscope is worth evaluating. Its focus on tracked content, topic exploration, and optimization suits teams that care about maintaining quality over time.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">SERP research combined with writing and GEO workflows</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, Frase is a strong candidate. Its current platform connects article creation, auditing, SEO and GEO scoring, AI visibility, and CMS publishing.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">content strategy and topical authority</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, MarketMuse deserves a closer look. Its site inventory, tracked topics, briefs, and strategy documents address decisions beyond a single article.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">lower cost content optimization</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, NeuronWriter starts at $23 monthly and gives users several tiers before reaching enterprise style pricing.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">broader SEO work</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, Semrush may make more sense if you also need competitor analysis, keyword research, technical auditing, and rank tracking.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">structured agency briefs</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, Content Harmony has a clear research, brief, and grading workflow.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">keyword clustering and research</strong><span data-lexical-text="true">, WriterZen offers a different value proposition, especially because its current pricing uses one time payments.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The top Surfer SEO alternative therefore depends on the job you need done.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Do not ask only, "Which tool has the most features?"</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Ask:</span></p><ol class="list-decimal ml-4 mb-2" dir="auto"><li value="1" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Where does our content process slow down?</span></li><li value="2" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Which steps require separate software?</span></li><li value="3" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> How many articles do we create each month?</span></li><li value="4" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Do we need writing or only optimization?</span></li><li value="5" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Do we need keyword research?</span></li><li value="6" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Will several writers or clients use the account?</span></li><li value="7" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Do we need Google Search Console, WordPress, or Shopify integrations?</span></li><li value="8" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> Are we measuring traditional rankings, AI visibility, or both?</span></li><li value="9" class="ml-1"><span data-lexical-text="true"> What will the platform actually cost at our volume?</span></li></ol><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The answer becomes much clearer after those questions.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For teams that want to combine research, SERP analysis, AI generation, EEAT analysis, on page optimization, humanization, and publishing, </span><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Rext AI</strong><span data-lexical-text="true"> is worth testing alongside the dedicated optimization tools above. Its current pricing starts at $32 per month, so you can compare the actual workflow and output rather than choosing from feature lists alone.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">The key takeaway is simple: choose a platform around your workflow, not somebody else's "best tools" ranking. Surfer remains capable, but Clearscope, Frase, MarketMuse, NeuronWriter, Semrush, Content Harmony, WriterZen, and newer AI first platforms solve different parts of the content process.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Test two or three options with the same keyword and article. Compare research quality, editing time, optimization guidance, final output, and publishing effort. That small test will tell you far more than a feature checklist.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">If you want research, writing, optimization, and publishing in a more connected workflow, </span><a href="https://app.rext.ai/signup" class="text-primary hover:underline cursor-pointer"><span data-lexical-text="true">start with a free trial</span></a><span data-lexical-text="true"> and judge the platform using a real article you already plan to publish.</span></p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">12. Frequently Asked Questions</strong></h2><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">What is the best alternative to Surfer SEO?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">There is no universal best option. Clearscope suits editorial optimization, Frase combines research and AI content workflows, MarketMuse focuses on strategy, NeuronWriter offers lower cost optimization, and Semrush connects content with a broader SEO toolkit.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Choose based on the problem you need to solve rather than the number of features.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Is there a free alternative to Surfer SEO?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Yes, some tools offer free access or trials rather than permanently free full replacements. MarketMuse currently provides a Free plan with 10 queries per month. Frase offers a seven day trial, NeuronWriter offers a seven day Gold trial, and several other platforms provide trial access.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Always check current limits before choosing a free Surfer SEO alternative because free plans can change.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">What should I look for when choosing a Surfer SEO competitor?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Look for accurate SERP analysis, useful content scoring, keyword research, search intent guidance, content briefs, AI writing where needed, integrations, transparent limits, and pricing that works at your publishing volume.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">For larger teams, also consider collaboration, API access, client reporting, workspaces, and CMS publishing.</span></p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 scroll-mt-20" dir="auto"><strong class="font-bold" data-lexical-text="true">Is Semrush better than Surfer SEO for content optimization?</strong></h3><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">They serve overlapping but different needs. Surfer specializes heavily in content optimization and related workflows. Semrush covers a much wider SEO ecosystem, including keyword research, competitor research, auditing, rank tracking, and content tools.</span></p><p class="mb-2" dir="auto"><span data-lexical-text="true">Semrush may make more sense when you want broader SEO capabilities. A focused content platform may be simpler if optimization is your main need.</span></p>"`;

exports[`surfer-seo-alternatives.md round-trips the same on every Lexical version: markdown 1`] = `
"# 8 Best Surfer SEO Alternatives for Content Optimization

 If you are comparing Surfer SEO alternatives, focus on more than a content score. The strongest choice should fit your full workflow, including SERP research, keyword analysis, content briefs, writing, optimization, publishing, and increasingly, visibility across AI search.

Surfer remains a capable content optimization platform; however, different teams need different things. Some want lower pricing. Others need deeper content strategy, stronger keyword research, automated publishing, AI writing, or tools built around Google and generative search together.

This guide compares nine options and related platforms based on what they actually help you accomplish, rather than treating every SEO tool as interchangeable.

## **1. Why Look for a Surfer SEO Alternative?**

Surfer SEO helps writers and SEO teams create content based on what already performs in search. Its platform includes content optimization, keyword research, auditing, AI writing, and AI visibility features. New accounts can currently test its Pro plan through a seven-day trial; the core idea is useful. Enter a target query, study the SERPs, identify relevant terms and topics, then improve your page against those signals.

So why switch?

Usually, the problem is not that Surfer cannot optimize content. The issue is that different businesses have different workflows, so you may want an alternative to Surfer SEO if you need:

-   Lower monthly costs
-   More articles within your budget
-   Built-in keyword research
-   Stronger content planning
-   AI-assisted drafting
-   Automated CMS publishing
-   Better agency workflows
-   More flexible team access
-   AI search monitoring
-   A different approach to content scoring

There is another practical reason that a high optimization score does not automatically make a page useful or rankable.

Content still needs to satisfy search intent, show real expertise, answer the query clearly, and offer something that competing pages do not. Google does not rank a page simply because an SEO content editor gives it a high score.

This is a common mistake when teams first adopt content optimization software. Writers start chasing every recommended phrase instead of asking whether the extra text helps the reader.

Treat optimization scores as guidance, not a finish line.

## **2. What Should You Look for in the Best Surfer SEO Alternatives?**

The best Surfer alternatives should solve a real weakness in your current workflow.

Before comparing prices, write down what you actually need the software to do. This prevents you from paying for a large platform when you only use two features.

### **SERP analysis**

A useful SERP analysis tool should help you understand the pages competing for your query.

Look beyond word counts. You want information that helps answer questions such as:

-   What topics appear repeatedly?
-   What does the searcher expect?
-   Which competitors should you compare against?
-   Which subtopics are missing?
-   How comprehensive does the page need to be?

### **Content scoring**

A content scoring tool gives writers a measurable optimization target that can make editing faster, especially across a large content team. But the score should support editorial judgment rather than replace it.

A page can hit an excellent score and still be weak if it lacks original insight, uses awkward keywords, or fails to answer the searcher's main question.

### **Keyword research and clustering**

Some platforms focus mainly on individual articles, and others combine content optimization with keyword research, keyword clustering, and topic discovery.

The second approach may make more sense when you are building topical authority rather than optimizing one page at a time.

### **AI writing**

AI writing can reduce production time, but volume alone has little value.

Look at what happens before and after generations. Does the software research the topic? Can it build a useful outline? Does it support your brand voice? Can you review SEO recommendations before publishing?

A good workflow should make human review easier, not encourage blind publishing.

### **Content briefs**

Agencies and editorial teams should pay close attention to content briefs.

A useful content brief gives a writer direction before the first sentence gets written. It may cover search intent, headings, competing pages, important topics, questions, keywords, and other requirements.

That saves editors from fixing strategic problems after a 2,000-word draft already exists.

### **AI search visibility**

Traditional Google rankings are no longer the only discovery surface worth watching.

Content may also appear or receive citations in Google AI Overviews and platforms such as ChatGPT and other AI search experiences.

Do not assume that an "AI optimized" label guarantees citations. No SEO optimization software can guarantee that an AI system will cite a particular page.

Instead, look for tools that help you create clear, well-structured, well-sourced content and measure visibility where relevant.

### **Workflow and integrations**

Finally, consider what happens after optimization.

If your team writes in Google Docs, works inside WordPress, manages Shopify sites, or depends on Google Search Console, integrations can save significant time.

The best software is often the one people actually use consistently.

![Image showing Rext AI features](https://juvrqxhye2tzsl8t.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/ChatGPT-Image-Sep-23--2026--01_30_54-PM-bCLqeRNEJxySx5GhCEjX25O0KFCrwq.png "Image showing Rext AI features")

## **3. Rext AI, An AI-Focused Alternative to Surfer SEO**

[Rext AI](https://rext.ai/) takes a broader approach to the SEO content workflow. Instead of stopping at recommendations inside a content editor, it combines keyword research, SERP analysis, outline generation, article generation, EEAT analysis, on-page SEO, humanization, and optional CMS publishing within one workflow. 

That makes it worth considering when your main problem is not simply optimizing an existing draft. It is more relevant when you want to reduce the number of separate steps needed to move from a keyword to a publishable article.

### **Key Features**

Its current feature set includes:

-   Unlimited keyword research across paid plans
-   Analysis of the top 10 SERP results
-   EEAT injection and analysis
-   On-page SEO optimization
-   Outline and article generation
-   A humanization pass
-   Optional AI image generation
-   CMS publishing, including WordPress
-   Multiple workspaces on higher plans

A useful distinction is the credit system. The company publishes the credit cost for individual actions instead of describing usage only through vague word limits. A standard SEO article is listed at 15 credits, while optional actions can use additional credits. 

For teams producing content at scale, that makes monthly output easier to estimate.

### **Pricing Plans**

Current monthly [pricing](https://rext.ai/pricing) starts at:

-   **Starter:** $39 per month, 400 credits
-   **Growth:** $89 per month, 1,000 credits
-   **Pro:** $189 per month, 2,400 credits
-   **Agency:** $399 per month, 5,500 credits

Annual billing currently reduces paid plan pricing by 20%. The platform also offers a free trial without requiring a card to start. 

### **Best For**

This approach makes the most sense for marketers, publishers, bloggers, and agencies that want research, generation, optimization, and publishing closer together.

It may be less relevant if you already have a mature writing stack and only want a dedicated optimization editor.

## **4. Clearscope, A Surfer SEO Competitor for Content Optimization**

Clearscope is a well-established option for teams that care heavily about content quality, optimization, and structured editorial workflows.

Its current offering has also expanded beyond traditional SEO. Clearscope now describes its plans around both SEO and AI search visibility, with tracked prompts and pages included in its packages.

That makes the platform particularly interesting for established content teams that want to monitor content rather than optimize a draft once and forget about it.

### **Key Features**

Clearscope focuses on areas such as:

-   Content optimization
-   Topic exploration
-   Content drafts
-   Page tracking
-   AI search visibility
-   Prompt tracking
-   Unlimited users
-   Unlimited projects

One benefit for larger editorial teams is its unlimited user model. You do not necessarily want pricing to jump every time another editor, strategist, or writer needs access.

### **Pricing Plans**

Clearscope currently lists three primary plans:

-   **Essentials:** $129 per month
-   **Business:** $399 per month
-   **Enterprise:** Custom pricing

Essentials currently includes 50 tracked prompts, 50 pages, 20 monthly Topic Explorations, and 20 monthly Drafts. Business increases the tracked prompts and pages to 300 each and adds a dedicated account manager. A 14-day free trial is available. 

That places Clearscope toward the premium end of this comparison.

### **Best For**

Clearscope is worth considering for editorial and content teams that place a high value on optimization quality and do not need the cheapest possible platform.

If budget is your biggest constraint, lower-priced alternatives may make more sense.

![Image showing features of different Ai writing tools of surfer alternatives](https://juvrqxhye2tzsl8t.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/clear-scope-vs-frasevs-maeketmuse-vs-newrin-writers-50rf5LIUaGqZ8kyuZNlE0cPiStTnaa.png "Image showing features of different Ai writing tools of surfer alternatives")

## **5. Frase, A Surfer SEO Alternative for SERP Research and AI Writing**

Frase has evolved from an SEO research and optimization product into what it calls a content operating system for AI search.

Its current workflow combines content creation with SEO and GEO scoring, publishing, auditing, and AI visibility features. The Starter plan can publish directly to WordPress, Webflow, Sanity, Wix, or FraseCMS.

That combination makes Frase attractive when research and writing need to happen in the same environment.

### **Key Features**

Depending on the plan, Frase can support:

-   SEO and GEO scoring
-   Content research
-   Content optimization
-   AI-assisted writing
-   Content auditing
-   AI visibility monitoring
-   CMS publishing
-   Content decay monitoring

The practical advantage is workflow continuity. Research does not have to live in one platform, the brief in another, and publishing somewhere else.

That can matter more than having the longest feature list.

### **Pricing Plans**

Frase currently lists its Starter plan at $49 per month when billed monthly, or $39 per month with annual billing. It includes one seat, one site, 10 articles, and 50 audit pages per month. A seven-day trial is available without a credit card.

Higher plans increase capacity and are aimed at content teams with larger workflows.

### **Best For**

Frase fits writers and teams that want SERP research, optimization, drafting, and publishing connected in one workflow.

It is also worth exploring if GEO scoring and AI visibility are becoming part of your content process.

## **6. MarketMuse, A Surfer SEO Alternative for Content Strategy**

MarketMuse approaches SEO from a different angle.

While individual page optimization matters, MarketMuse places substantial emphasis on your broader content inventory, topical coverage, gaps, and content strategy.

This distinction becomes important when a site already has hundreds or thousands of pages.

At that point, asking "How should we optimize this article?" is only part of the problem.

You also need to ask:

-   Which topic should we cover next?
-   Where is our authority strongest?
-   Which existing page deserves an update?
-   What are we missing?
-   Which content opportunity deserves resources?

MarketMuse is designed around those larger content decisions.

### **Key Features**

Its current platform includes:

-   Topic Navigator
-   Keyword research
-   SERP X ray
-   SERP Heatmap
-   Site Heatmap
-   Content inventories
-   Tracked topics
-   Content briefs
-   Strategy documents
-   Content optimization

MarketMuse says it uses proprietary data and topic modeling rather than relying only on generic API data.

### **Pricing Plans**

MarketMuse currently offers:

-   **Free:** 10 queries per month
-   **Optimize:** includes 100 tracked topics and five briefs monthly
-   **Research:** includes 1,000 tracked topics and 10 briefs
-   **Strategy:** includes 10,000 tracked topics and 20 briefs

Its public pricing page currently directs users to book a demo for paid tiers rather than displaying dollar prices in the retrieved plan summary. 

The free level is notable because users searching for a Surfer SEO free alternative can explore parts of the platform before moving into a paid workflow.

### **Best For**

MarketMuse is best suited to content strategists, established publishers, and larger teams that need to decide what to create and update across an entire content library.

If you only need a simple editor for one article at a time, it may be more platform than you need.

## **7. NeuronWriter, An Affordable Surfer SEO Alternative**

NeuronWriter stands out mainly because it offers a wide range of SEO and AI features at comparatively accessible starting prices.

Its platform combines content optimization with AI writing, content planning, integrations, plagiarism checks on qualifying plans, and AI visibility monitoring.

That makes it one of the more interesting affordable Surfer SEO alternatives for small teams.

### **Key Features**

Depending on your plan, features include:

-   Content Writer analyses
-   AI writing credits
-   Content planning
-   AI templates
-   Content Designer
-   Plagiarism checks
-   Google Search Console integration
-   WordPress integration
-   Shopify integration
-   API access on qualifying plans
-   AI monitored questions

NeuronWriter also lists monitoring across Google, Google AI Overviews, AI Mode, ChatGPT, and Perplexity through its AI Monitoring offering.

### **Pricing Plans**

Current monthly prices are:

-   **Bronze:** $23
-   **Silver:** $45
-   **Gold:** $69
-   **Platinum:** $93
-   **Diamond:** $117

Annual billing reduces those monthly equivalent prices to $19, $37, $57, $77, and $97 respectively. A seven day trial under Gold plan terms is available. 

The Gold plan is where several advanced capabilities become available, including integrations, advanced AI templates, plagiarism checking, and Content Designer.

### **Best For**

NeuronWriter deserves consideration from freelancers, bloggers, small agencies, and site owners who want NLP SEO tools and content optimization without starting at a high monthly price.

When comparing Surfer SEO vs NeuronWriter, pay close attention to limits and workflow rather than price alone.

![Image showing features of different Ai writing tools of surfer alternatives](https://juvrqxhye2tzsl8t.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/semrush--suurfe-and-content-harmion-MBqCryTBzwIa7jyieYQIxfLpdJDq09.png "Image showing features of different Ai writing tools of surfer alternatives")

## **8. Semrush SEO Writing Assistant vs Surfer SEO**

Semrush is the broadest SEO ecosystem in this comparison.

That makes Semrush vs Surfer SEO slightly different from comparing two dedicated content editors.

Surfer centers heavily on content optimization and related content workflows. Semrush covers a much wider SEO stack, including keyword research, competitor research, site auditing, position tracking, content tools, and more.

For content specifically, there are two offerings worth understanding.

The SEO Writing Assistant evaluates areas such as SEO, readability, tone, and originality. Semrush also offers a newer Content Toolkit for ideation, briefs, AI content creation, optimization, and publishing. 

### **Key Features**

The content ecosystem includes capabilities such as:

-   Topic discovery
-   SEO brief generation
-   AI article creation
-   Content optimization
-   Brand voice
-   SEO recommendations
-   AI rewriting
-   WordPress publishing
-   SERP backed optimization
-   Broader keyword and competitor data

The bigger advantage appears when your team already uses Semrush.

Adding content tools to an existing SEO workflow may be simpler than adopting another standalone platform.

### **Pricing Plans**

The Semrush Content Toolkit currently costs $60 per month and offers a seven day free trial. It includes unlimited standard articles, five SEO boosted articles per month, SEO briefs, content ideas, optimization, AI rewriting, and WordPress export. 

The separate SEO Toolkit currently starts at $139.95 per month for Pro, while Guru costs $249.95 and Business costs $499.95 monthly. SEO Writing Assistant is included at the Guru level according to Semrush's current plan documentation.

This distinction matters. Do not assume every Semrush content feature comes with its cheapest SEO subscription.

### **Best For**

Semrush makes the most sense when content optimization is only one part of your SEO work.

If you also need keyword research, technical SEO, competitor analysis, and rank tracking, consolidating tools may be useful.

If you only want a focused content optimization experience, a dedicated platform may feel simpler.

## **9. Content Harmony and WriterZen as Surfer SEO Competitors**

Not every Surfer SEO competitor tries to solve the same problem.

Content Harmony and WriterZen illustrate this well. One places greater emphasis on structured content workflows and briefs. The other has strong keyword research and clustering functionality.

### **Content Harmony**

Content Harmony is built around repeatable content workflows.

Each Content Workflow includes a Keyword Report, Content Brief, and Content Grader. This creates a logical process from research to instructions to final optimization. 

**Key Features**

-   Keyword reports
-   Search intent research
-   Content briefs
-   Content grading
-   Unlimited users
-   Unlimited projects
-   Rollover credits
-   Team training

For agencies, unlimited users and projects can be particularly useful. A cheap base plan becomes less attractive if every additional team member creates another fee.

#### **Pricing Plans**

Pricing scales by monthly Content Workflows:

-   5 workflows: $50 per month
-   12 workflows: $99
-   25 workflows: $199
-   50 workflows: $299
-   100 workflows: $599
-   150 workflows: $799
-   Enterprise: from $1,000 per month

There is also a $10 trial that provides 10 workflow credits and does not automatically convert into a subscription. 

#### **Best For**

Content Harmony is particularly relevant for agencies and content teams that need standardized briefs and a clear handoff between strategists, writers, and editors.

### **WriterZen**

WriterZen takes a more keyword centered approach.

It is useful when your challenge begins before the writing stage. Instead of simply asking how to optimize one article, you can research keywords and group related opportunities before building the content.

#### **Key Features**

Its current plans advertise capabilities such as:

-   Keyword research
-   Keyword clustering
-   Keyword lists
-   Keyword Explorer
-   Content Creator
-   AI writing on qualifying plans
-   Plagiarism checking
-   Topic discovery
-   Team collaboration

#### **Pricing Plans**

WriterZen currently promotes one time pricing rather than a standard monthly subscription.

Its Keyword Research package is listed at $135 one time, while All In One Basic costs $270 one time. The latter adds Content Creator functionality, up to 50 articles per month, unlimited AI writing, and plagiarism checking. That pricing structure is unusual in a category dominated by subscriptions.

#### **Best For**

WriterZen is worth considering when keyword discovery and keyword clustering are major parts of your workflow.

It may be particularly attractive to people who dislike adding another recurring software subscription.

## **10. Surfer SEO Alternatives Comparison: Features, Pricing and Best Use Cases**

There is no single feature that determines the right platform.

Use this comparison as a starting point, then test your shortlist with the type of content you actually produce.

| Tool | Best For | SERP/SEO Analysis | AI Writing | Broader Planning | Starting Price |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Rext AI | End to end Complete SEO workflow | Yes | Yes | Strong | $32/mo |
| Clearscope | Editorial optimization | Yes | Draft workflow | Yes | $129/mo |
| Frase | Research, writing and GEO workflow | Yes | Yes | Yes | $49/mo monthly |
| MarketMuse | Content strategy and topical planning | Yes | Optimization focused | Strong | Free tier |
| NeuronWriter | Affordable optimization | Yes | Yes | Yes | $23/mo |
| Semrush Content Toolkit | Wider SEO and content workflow | Yes | Yes | Strong | $60/mo |
| Content Harmony | Briefs and agency workflows | Yes | No core focus | Strong | $50/mo |
| WriterZen | Keyword research and clustering | Yes | Yes on qualifying plan | Strong | $135 one time |

Pricing and features change, sometimes quickly. The figures above reflect publicly available pricing checked in September 2026.

A better way to choose is to identify your bottleneck.

**If writing takes too long:** prioritize an AI SEO tool that connects research, outlining, generation, and optimization.

**If writers miss search intent:** prioritize SERP research and strong content briefs.

**If your editors spend hours fixing drafts:** prioritize clear grading and optimization guidance.

**If you do not know what to publish:** prioritize keyword research, topic discovery, clustering, and content gap analysis.

**If you manage many clients:** consider workspaces, users, API integrations, reporting, and publishing workflow.

**If you already have hundreds of articles:** content inventory, auditing, performance analysis, and planning become more valuable than another writing interface.

This is also where buying based on a feature checklist can go wrong.

Imagine an agency publishes 80 articles per month. A $30 tool may sound cheaper, but not if the team spends another 20 minutes moving every article between research, writing, optimization, and WordPress.

Those 20 minutes become more than 26 hours across 80 articles.

Workflow cost matters alongside subscription cost.

## **11. Which Surfer SEO Alternative Should You Choose?**

Start with what you want to improve.

For an **end to end AI content workflow**, look for software that can move from keyword and SERP research into drafting, optimization, and publishing without unnecessary handoffs.

For **editorial optimization**, Clearscope is worth evaluating. Its focus on tracked content, topic exploration, and optimization suits teams that care about maintaining quality over time. 

For **SERP research combined with writing and GEO workflows**, Frase is a strong candidate. Its current platform connects article creation, auditing, SEO and GEO scoring, AI visibility, and CMS publishing. 

For **content strategy and topical authority**, MarketMuse deserves a closer look. Its site inventory, tracked topics, briefs, and strategy documents address decisions beyond a single article.

For **lower cost content optimization**, NeuronWriter starts at $23 monthly and gives users several tiers before reaching enterprise style pricing.

For **broader SEO work**, Semrush may make more sense if you also need competitor analysis, keyword research, technical auditing, and rank tracking.

For **structured agency briefs**, Content Harmony has a clear research, brief, and grading workflow.

For **keyword clustering and research**, WriterZen offers a different value proposition, especially because its current pricing uses one time payments.

The top Surfer SEO alternative therefore depends on the job you need done.

Do not ask only, "Which tool has the most features?"

Ask:

1.  Where does our content process slow down?
2.  Which steps require separate software?
3.  How many articles do we create each month?
4.  Do we need writing or only optimization?
5.  Do we need keyword research?
6.  Will several writers or clients use the account?
7.  Do we need Google Search Console, WordPress, or Shopify integrations?
8.  Are we measuring traditional rankings, AI visibility, or both?
9.  What will the platform actually cost at our volume?

The answer becomes much clearer after those questions.

For teams that want to combine research, SERP analysis, AI generation, EEAT analysis, on page optimization, humanization, and publishing, **Rext AI** is worth testing alongside the dedicated optimization tools above. Its current pricing starts at $32 per month, so you can compare the actual workflow and output rather than choosing from feature lists alone.

The key takeaway is simple: choose a platform around your workflow, not somebody else's "best tools" ranking. Surfer remains capable, but Clearscope, Frase, MarketMuse, NeuronWriter, Semrush, Content Harmony, WriterZen, and newer AI first platforms solve different parts of the content process.

Test two or three options with the same keyword and article. Compare research quality, editing time, optimization guidance, final output, and publishing effort. That small test will tell you far more than a feature checklist.

If you want research, writing, optimization, and publishing in a more connected workflow, [start with a free trial](https://app.rext.ai/signup) and judge the platform using a real article you already plan to publish.

## **12. Frequently Asked Questions**

### **What is the best alternative to Surfer SEO?**

There is no universal best option. Clearscope suits editorial optimization, Frase combines research and AI content workflows, MarketMuse focuses on strategy, NeuronWriter offers lower cost optimization, and Semrush connects content with a broader SEO toolkit.

Choose based on the problem you need to solve rather than the number of features.

### **Is there a free alternative to Surfer SEO?**

Yes, some tools offer free access or trials rather than permanently free full replacements. MarketMuse currently provides a Free plan with 10 queries per month. Frase offers a seven day trial, NeuronWriter offers a seven day Gold trial, and several other platforms provide trial access. 

Always check current limits before choosing a free Surfer SEO alternative because free plans can change.

### **What should I look for when choosing a Surfer SEO competitor?**

Look for accurate SERP analysis, useful content scoring, keyword research, search intent guidance, content briefs, AI writing where needed, integrations, transparent limits, and pricing that works at your publishing volume.

For larger teams, also consider collaboration, API access, client reporting, workspaces, and CMS publishing.

### **Is Semrush better than Surfer SEO for content optimization?**

They serve overlapping but different needs. Surfer specializes heavily in content optimization and related workflows. Semrush covers a much wider SEO ecosystem, including keyword research, competitor research, auditing, rank tracking, and content tools.

Semrush may make more sense when you want broader SEO capabilities. A focused content platform may be simpler if optimization is your main need."
